# ─── Assets: protect the repo from the 3.4 GB raw/unused tree ─────────────────
# The runtime-used asset set (~604 curated files, each < 100 MB) is ALREADY tracked
# and STAYS in git — .gitignore never untracks already-tracked files. These rules
# only stop the multi-GB UNTRACKED tree from being staged via `git add .`.
# To add a NEW used asset on purpose:  git add -f <path>   (or add a ! negation here).
# See GIT_ASSET_STRATEGY.md.
#
# Raw / large source formats anywhere (never loaded at runtime):
*.bin
*.fbx
*.zip
# The asset working tree (curated used files already committed remain tracked):
/public/assets/
# Scratch / source models outside the runtime tree:
/src/assets/
